        "id": 2007917
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-06-28T12:17:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, you are right. I am talking about the same sequence.\nThe problem is we use the same VolumeInfo reference which is stored in mVolumes, so in IVoldListener#onVolumeStateChanged (Ref: https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:frameworks/base/services/core/java/com/android/server/StorageManagerService.java;l\u003d1473?q\u003dStorageManagerService\u0026ss\u003dandroid%2Fplatform%2Fsuperproject), the VolumeInfos are fetched from the mVolumes. So we if update the reference for particular volId, then the member variable values (which includes mountUserId) also change.\nAnd if Line#1473 is executed before actually the values are supposed to change, then the broadcasts will be sent for wrong values for a Volume.\nWe have to find a better way of solving the issue",
      "parentUuid": "660e9f15_852ca0f1",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1355,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1355,
        "endChar": 66
      },
      "revId": "afdaf35814305edfad20f7b45f84df7ce864959a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e8d2645a_d1291b5e",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/StorageManagerService.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1355,
      "author": {
        "id": 2007917
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-06-29T16:48:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I have solution in mind, please let me know if that works.\nSo our main problem is to send the correct broadcast to the correct user, and trigger point of that is in IVoldListener#onVolumeChanged.\nAt Line#1477 we create a copy of VolumeInfo which is used for broadcast.\nWhat I have in my mind is if we can add userId as an extra parameter in IVoldListener#onVolumeChanged and update the copy, then we won\u0027t run into this problem (as the reference in mVolumes stays unchanged). Also, in this way we can keep maybeRemountVolumes unchanged and still resolve the issue.",
      "parentUuid": "3839a1f3_0e005cf1",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1355,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1355,
        "endChar": 66
      },
      "revId": "afdaf35814305edfad20f7b45f84df7ce864959a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
